  "body": "## Result\n\nCloses the explicit source-XOR optimality handoff in Arham Tahir's merged PR #1898 / discussion #1579. In the generic common-B mutable-source connector, if the complete source-XOR interaction graph has k components, every restored finite word obeys\n\n- Q >= n+k;\n- X >= 2(n-k);\n- therefore 2Q+X >= 4n and the sharp X count at minimum Q=n+1 is 2(n-1).\n\nThe credited PR1898 construction attains the new lower bound; its construction and readout theorem are not claimed as new. The package also gives the sharp projected Q/X frontier, with unrestricted readouts, and a sufficient global unequal-price optimality cone. For n=5, complete prices b >= 34a+2x make 6b+96a+8x the global tariff minimum over all finite words. The fully expanded eight-factor abstract fixture has (b,a,x)=(86,2,2), exact optimum 724, and every Q>=7 competitor costs at least 738.\n\nThe key new proof is a source-matrix support-component potential. Adding one auxiliary edge between the XOR's row vertices makes the support partition invariant across the gate. Thus each historical component merge decreases the current component count by one, and final source restoration requires equally many increases. This covers arbitrary redundant/cancelling gates; a literal control never mixes all sources simultaneously. The query bound follows from full rank and zero-sum dependence separately in every historical component.\n\n## Evidence and reproduction\n\nOnly `research/mutable-source-connectivity-bound/` is added. Complete source pins, independently drawn SELECTION, TASK, written proof, deterministic receipts and explicit VERIFY hook are included.\n\n```sh\nuv run --python 3.12 --no-project python -I -O -B research/mutable-source-connectivity-bound/verify.py\nuv run --python 3.12 --no-project python scripts/research_package.py --package research/mutable-source-connectivity-bound\n```\n\nActually passed on CPython3.12.12/macOS arm64:\n\n- 242,940 single-gate GL1..4 transitions, with independent row-intersection oracle;\n- bounded closed-source-word census and 66 integer-partition witnesses for n=1..8;\n- complete free-linear dirty-state/noncommuting forward and inverse expansion;\n- 288 independently implemented dense forward/inverse cases, 40 dirty rows;\n- 12 primary and five independent semantic controls, including removal of an actual private uncompute leaf;\n- five focused CLI/source/receipt/relocation/regeneration tests;\n- `PASS_REGISTERED_RESEARCH_PACKAGE ... outcome=completed`.\n\nAn initial tuple/list receipt-comparison failure was corrected by canonical whole-JSON comparison; no proof-relevant receipt field is skipped. The parent separately reviewed the proof and replayed the final package before publication.\n\n## Scope and attribution\n\nThis is a written all-n proof with finite machine evidence, not formal-kernel acceptance. The price cone is sufficient, not the complete unequal-price classification. Abstract unit prices do not establish favorable tape costs, a selected-supplier caller, a paid moment improvement, physical runtime gain, or new kappa. All selected/frozen inputs remain unchanged; no selected cold replay or hosted-CI success is claimed.\n\nCredit Arham Tahir (PR1340, PR1370, PR1898), TennisBowling (PR1524), Ross Richardson (PR943/934), and the inherited shhxera/CubeJerry / Chafik Boukhalfa lineage. Exact heads are pinned; targeted live checks confirm all five direct predecessors merged at those heads. Cached overlap covered329openPRs and692discussions with full pagination and explicit freshness warnings; a targeted live all-state source-XOR search found34PRs and no same missing-lemma closure. Search is not a novelty certificate.\n\nIndependent seed `40c024ae825b6e48dce27fd8e1257c7b`, recursive-interfaces / connector-alphabet-change. Exact base `e112d71c8d7bb32435debcc54df932593dd8223a`. Scoped claim: #research-claim-and-completion-record\n\nPrepared for Adam Gall with substantial OpenAI Codex (GPT-6 Astra) assistance in proof, code, experiments and writing. Apache-2.0. No independent human review is claimed.\n\n## Research claim and completion record\n\nStatus: completed. The claim record is preserved here so this PR is self-contained. Historical coordination links in the committed research metadata refer to this record; the separate coordination discussion is being removed.\n\nDONE \u2014 [PR2064](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/2064), full commit `43ff11e0503dbc71d20e13177c144e962f521751`. Seed `40c024ae825b6e48dce27fd8e1257c7b`; exact base `e112d71c8d7bb32435debcc54df932593dd8223a`.\n\nThe all-n restored-source support-component proof establishes X>=2(n-k), Q>=n+k, hence sharp X=2(n-1) at minimum Q=n+1. This closes PR1898/discussion1579 source-XOR optimality handoff; its construction and readout theorem retain Arham Tahir credit. The projected Q/X frontier and a sufficient global unequal-price cone are also proved: for five sources b>=34a+2x yields exact tariff6b+96a+8x. Fully expanded eight-factor fixture (b,a,x)=(86,2,2) has global abstract optimum724; all Q>=7 cost>=738. No physical/supplier/kappa improvement is claimed.\n\nSource-bound CPython3.12.12 optimized and registered replay passes242940GLtransitions,66partitionwitnesses,12semanticcontrols,288independent dense forward/inverse pairs,5independentcontrols and5focusedtests. The parent separately reviewed the proof and replayed final bytes before publication. Reproduce: `uv run --python 3.12 --no-project python scripts/research_package.py --package research/mutable-source-connectivity-bound`. Formal-kernel, independent-human and hostedCI success are not claimed.\n\nCredit Arham Tahir(PR1340/1370/1898), TennisBowling(PR1524), Ross Richardson(PR943/934), shhxera/CubeJerry and Chafik Boukhalfa. Prepared for Adam Gall with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance; Apache-2.0. Original scope: paid elementary source-XOR extension, arbitrary readouts, all-n historical/current-component potential; claim expiry20:25UTC, now released.\n",
